Subject: R or S-plus code for scaled rectangle diagrams?
Message-ID: <20060602131545.601271008C52@mailgate.biostat.wustl.edu>

Does anyone know of an R or S-Plus function to draw scaled
rectangle diagrams?  This variation on Venn diagrams is described here:

 

Marshall, RJ.  Displaying clinical data relationships
using scaled rectangle diagrams.  Statist. Med. 2001;20:1077-1088.

 

http://www.health.auckland.ac.nz/population-health/epidemiology-biostats/span/sim_rectanglediagrams.pdf

 

Note to my academic colleagues: Given the algorithmic,
geometric, and graphical issues that Marshall
lays out, it seems to me that this would make a great programming project for
tormenting undergraduates.

 

