Kim,

  I think it is pretty easy if
you use the diff() function. Here's code to start with and the output.

cbind(a[c(1,diff(a$DOSE)) != 0,],ENDDATE=a[c(diff(a$DOSE),1)
!= 0,3])

   ID DOSE      
DATE    ENDDATE 

 1  1 0.25 01/01/2006 01/02/2006

 3  1 0.50 01/03/2006 01/03/2006

 4  1 0.25 01/04/2006 01/05/2006

 6  1 2.50 01/06/2006 01/07/2006

 8  1 0.25 01/08/2006 01/08/2006

 9  2 2.50 01/09/2006 01/11/2006

12  2 3.50 01/12/2006 01/12/2006

13  2 2.50 01/13/2006 01/14/2006

15  2 2.00 01/15/2006 01/16/2006

17  2 4.00 01/17/2006 01/17/2006

18  3 2.00 01/18/2006 01/18/2006

19  3 2.50 01/19/2006 01/20/2006

21  3 2.00 01/21/2006 01/22/2006

  The first selection extracts
the first value in any repeated sequence of DOSE, the second one extracts
the DATE of the last in a sequence of repeated values of DOSE. I only checked
for a change in DOSE, you will need to include a check for change in ID,
using the same diff logic on ID and the | logical operator.

